   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>
                        <seg type="published" function="context">
                            <quote>Meanwhile I have asked the printer to keep the type set, pending your reply.</quote>
                            <bibl>LI 106-7</bibl>
                        </seg>
                    </p>
                    <p>        	As you seem to want <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">continental notices</seg> I shall do all I can to that end. A notice will appear shortly in an <seg xml:id="seg2" type="note-anchor">Amsterdam paper</seg>.</p>
                    <p>        	My health is rather better but I shall never recover wholly in this dreadful climate.</p>
                    <closer>
                        <salute>                    	With kind regards</salute>
                        <salute>                                	sincerely yours</salute>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">                                            	James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                        <dateline>
                            <date when="1917-07-18">
                                <seg xml:id="seg3" type="note-anchor">18.7.1917</seg>
                            </date>
                        </dateline>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">Harriet Weaver wrote to JJ on <date when="1917-07-29">29 July 1917</date> about <name type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">A Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man</name>: “I think it would be useful to have as many foreign notices as possible” (Firth 173).</note>
                <note xml:id="note2" target="#seg2" type="commentary">Pieter Endt's review of <name type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">A Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man</name>, published under the pseudonym of Ed Coenraads, “Een Ierse schrijver” in <name type="work">De Nieuwe Gids</name> 33, x (<date when="1918-01">January 1918</date>): 516-19.</note>
                <note xml:id="note3" target="#seg3" type="commentary">Dated by JJ as <date when="1917-07-18">18 July 1917</date>, but postmarked <date when="1917-07-17">17 July 1917</date>.</note>
            </div>
      </body>
